cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GeoMix: A Bayesian Framework for Stratigraphic and Geotechnical Inference"
abstract: >
  GeoMix is a fully Bayesian hierarchical framework for jointly inferring
  geological stratigraphy and geotechnical properties from seismic and
  geotechnical data. It uses a Potts Markov random field to represent spatially
  coherent geology, class-specific Gaussian processes for geotechnical
  properties, and a grouped Vecchia approximation for scalable inference.
authors:
  - family-names: Wakefield
    given-names: Bradley
repository-code: "https://github.com/bradleywakefield/geomix-paper"
license: MIT
date-released: "2025-01-01"
keywords:
  - Bayesian inference
  - stratigraphy
  - geotechnical
  - Gaussian process
  - Potts model
  - Markov random field
  - Vecchia approximation
  - offshore wind
  - seismic interpretation
